<%# The Buy/Sell pair, defined once and rendered in two places: inside the primary cell below
    lg, and in the trailing actions column at lg. Two call sites, one definition, because these
    are the product's core transaction and a copy that drifts is worse here than anywhere.

    Both are the secondary button. They were a filled teal Buy beside a filled amber Sell,
    repeated down every row - two saturated fills per row, in two different hues, on the densest
    page in the app. Buy and Sell are told apart by their label and their arrow, not by colour,
    which is what design.md asks for anyway. The emphasis belongs to the confirm step in the
    order modal, where a single primary button sits alone.

    Buy is withheld for an archived stock - you may only sell out of one. %>
<div class="flex gap-2 <%= local_assigns[:class] %>">
  <% unless stock.archived? %>
    <%= link_to new_order_path(stock_id: stock.id, transaction_type: :buy),
                class: "tw-btn-secondary",
                data: { turbo_frame: "modal_frame", testid: "buy-stock-button" } do %>
      <%= lucide_icon("arrow-up", class: "size-4 shrink-0") %> Buy
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= link_to new_order_path(stock_id: stock.id, transaction_type: :sell),
              class: "tw-btn-secondary",
              data: { turbo_frame: "modal_frame", testid: "sell-stock-button" } do %>
    <%= lucide_icon("arrow-down", class: "size-4 shrink-0") %> Sell
  <% end %>
</div>
